  "question": {
    "html": "<p>A particle undergoes simple harmonic motion. Its maximum speed is <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"v_{\\text{max}}\"></span> and its maximum acceleration is <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"a_{\\text{max}}\"></span>. Which of the following is a correct expression for the period <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"T\"></span> of the particle's motion?</p><ol class=\"mcq-options\"><li data-label=\"A\"><p><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"T = 2\\pi \\sqrt{\\frac{v_{\\text{max}}}{a_{\\text{max}}}}\"></span></p></li><li data-label=\"B\"><p><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"T = 2\\pi \\frac{a_{\\text{max}}}{v_{\\text{max}}}\"></span></p></li><li data-label=\"C\"><p><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"T = 2\\pi \\frac{v_{\\text{max}}}{a_{\\text{max}}}\"></span></p></li><li data-label=\"D\"><p><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"T = \\frac{1}{2\\pi} \\frac{v_{\\text{max}}}{a_{\\text{max}}}\"></span></p></li></ol>"
  },
